{"uid":"src/css_box.c::calc_val","name":"calc_val","qualname":"calc_val","kind":"struct","file":"src/css_box.c","line":600,"end_line":600,"language":"c","signature":"typedef struct calc_val { double px; double em; double pct; int is_length; } calc_val;","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"`pct` is the percentage component, carried through the arithmetic exactly like `em` and for exactly the same reason: a calc() result is the affine combination a*1px + b*1em + c*1%, and CSS Values 4 section 10 lets an author mix all three.","description":"Collapsing the percentage at parse time is impossible -- its basis is the containing block, which the element-free cascade does not know -- so it travels symbolically to bx_lp_px, the one place a percentage becomes pixels.\n\nBefore this, calc() understood no percentage at all, so `width: calc(100% - 2rem)`\n-- the single most common responsive idiom on the web -- was dropped whole.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/css_box.c","members":["src/css_box.c::calc_val.px"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
